After merging origin/main (TE-1 /v1 escalation, 9959e8db/280059cc) onto the swap
lane: /chat's answer verdict now resolves the reviewer (architect_critic, the 27B),
so v1_escalation's comment "_architect_verdict always asks architect_general" no
longer held and its receipt would have labelled a 27B call as the consultant.
- chat_review._architect_verdict gains an optional role (default: reviewer binding).
- v1_escalation: `auto` keeps /chat's target (reviewer); `x_escalation=
  architect_general` (UFH-13 A2) pins the verdict to the consultant, as it pins
  every consultant call; the step records the role actually asked.
- test_v1_escalation: auto expects architect_critic for the verdict; pinned-arm
  expectations unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FKXdQsgLuwnFVWQ3npGfrJ
